      {
        "Id": "66cc5bc491c34ef6a0a4b47c2bff0f52",
        "Title": "HOW TO USE:  0 = the units you want:  MM,  CM,  M,  FT-IN (feet-inches),  FT (decimal feet).  1 = project units (Manage > Project Units),  2 = every dimension type (linear, radial, diameter, arc, spot elevation) so the dimensions in all views change,  3 = area m2/ft2 + volume m3/ft3.  4 = only dimension types whose name contains these words (comma list, ALL = all).  5 = rounding: blank = normal, 0 / 1 / 2 decimals, feet-inches 8 = 1/8 inch.  6 = show mm / cm / m after the number.  7 RUN False = preview, True = change.  Only the display changes.  Ctrl+Z undoes.",
        "DescriptionText": "",
